From 9cfd26e354ca19253db9a2057dca0d1050ce7bc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:01:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] bcmbt: power and clocks for UART-attached Broadcom
 Bluetooth

The DT describes these controllers (brcm,bcm43438-bt and relatives) as a
child of their UART node with an lpo clock, vbat/vddio supplies and
shutdown/device-wakeup GPIOs. The UART driver enumerates no children, so
nothing powered them. bcmbt finds such nodes from simplebus, enables what
they reference and exposes dev.bcmbt.N.power (0/1/2 = off/on/cycle) and
dev.bcmbt.N.tty (the parent UART's callout device). Patchram and the hand-off
to ng_h4 are userland's, like iwmbtfw for USB.

Tested on a Banana Pi M64 (AP6212): enables the aw_rtc 32 kHz fanout and the
module supplies, the chip then boots its patchram and l2ping reaches a laptop.

Signed-off-by: Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
