+.\"
+.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
+.\"
+.\" Copyright (c) 2026 Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
+.\"
+.Dd September 26, 2026
+.Dt BCMBT 4
+.Os
+.Sh NAME
+.Nm bcmbt
+.Nd power control for UART-attached Broadcom Bluetooth controllers
+.Sh SYNOPSIS
+To load the driver as a module at boot time, place the following line in
+.Xr loader.conf 5 :
+.Bd -literal -offset indent
+bcmbt_load="YES"
+.Ed
+.Sh DESCRIPTION
+The
+.Nm
+driver handles the devicetree nodes that describe a Broadcom Bluetooth
+controller attached to a UART
+.Po
+.Qq brcm,bcm43438-bt
+and related compatibles, as children of the UART node
+.Pc .
+On attach it enables the resources such a node references: the
+.Qq lpo
+clock, the
+.Qq vbat-supply
+and
+.Qq vddio-supply
+regulators, and the
+.Qq shutdown-gpios
+and
+.Qq device-wakeup-gpios
+lines, and then powers the controller on.
+.Pp
+Loading the controller's firmware and attaching it to the Bluetooth stack
+is done from userland by
+.Xr bcmbtattach 8 ,
+through
+.Xr ng_h4 4 .
+.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
+.Bl -tag -width indent
+.It Va dev.bcmbt.%d.power
+Writing 0 powers the controller off, 1 on, and 2 power-cycles it.
+Reads return 0 or 1.
+.It Va dev.bcmbt.%d.tty
+The callout device of the UART the controller is attached to, for example
+.Pa cuau1 .
+.El
+.Sh SEE ALSO
+.Xr ng_h4 4 ,
+.Xr ng_hci 4 ,
+.Xr bcmbtattach 8
+.Sh AUTHORS
+.An Andrey Bodrov Aq Mt ap.bodrov@gmail.com
